<section class="content" id="technical-details" aria-labelledby="tech-heading">
  <h2 id="tech-heading">Technical Specifications & IANA Timezone Database Metadata</h2>
  <p>
    Software developers require exact database keys to perform automated timezone calculations across enterprise systems.
  </p>
  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Canonical Identifiers</h3>
      <p>The primary IANA time zone key for Moscow is <code>Europe/Moscow</code>. Additional Russian MSK aliases include <code>Europe/Simferopol</code> and <code>Europe/Kirov</code>.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>ISO 8601 Offset Representation</h3>
      <p>MSK is expressed in ISO 8601 string formats as <code>+03:00</code> (e.g., <code>2026-07-30T17:00:00+03:00</code>).</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>POSIX Timezone Specification</h3>
      <p>The standard POSIX string for Moscow Standard Time is <code>MSK-3</code>, denoting standard time 3 hours ahead of UTC without DST shifts.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Railways & Federal Infrastructure Sync</h3>
      <p>Russian Railways (RZD) and federal aviation networks coordinate timetables using local time synchronized to MSK atomic standards.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

